[h3]Raiding Focus[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Token Abduction[/b] (new focus): capped at 5% of a target's population, with no escalation. Once you hit the cap your only option is switching to plundering. Finishing a raid grants 12 months of your unity income.
[*][b]Reaping[/b] is no longer the default unless your civic is built around it: Harvesting Protocol, Harvest Incorporated or Ravager Swarm. Everyone else who qualifies picks it themselves.
[*]Pop raiding is now called [b]Abduction[/b]. Robot Raiding's first option now reads [b]Organics and Robots[/b].
[/list]

[h3]Despoliation Traditions[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Forward Raiding Base[/b] reworked. Instead of skimming 3% from every nearby colony each cycle, each non-ally colony within 3 systems now has a 1 in 12 chance of being raided for 60% of a month's output.
[/list]

[h3]Privateer Enclave[/h3]
[list]
[*]Nomads can now be privateer patrons. The system's owner and any nomad holding a waystation in that system both count, so an enclave can have one of each, and both are paid dividends.
[*]An enclave with no patrons left stops paying dividends.
[/list]

[h3]Fixes[/h3]
[list]
[*]The raiding report no longer appears when a war ends.
[*]The opportunistic raiding prompt no longer appears twice for the same target.
[*]Raiding is no longer blocked when you declare a new war on an empire you recently fought.
[/list]
